WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.900
Analysis of Competing Hypotheses, often called ACH,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:09.300
encourages analysts to identify multiple plausible explanations and evaluate how evidence supports or contradicts each one.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.500
Rather than asking which explanation feels most appealing,

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.900
ACH asks which explanation is least inconsistent with the available evidence.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.300
That shift helps reduce confirmation bias.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.500
ACH works best when analysts include alternatives they might otherwise dismiss too early.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
The process encourages comparison, transparency,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.900
and disciplined attention to contradictory evidence.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.900
The output is not certainty.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:36.100
The output is a clearer view of which explanations fit the evidence better,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.300
which evidence matters most, and where uncertainty remains.
